{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BipartiteGraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The invariant is the type: every initializer from unchecked input is failable, and a mutation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that would break it traps (whether an edge may be inserted is an O(1) test with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"side(of:)"},{"text":").","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Storage and mutation costs are ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedAdjacencyList"},{"text":"‘s: vertex indices are slots","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order), edge indices are positions, and a removal moves the last slot or edge into","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the hole, so orders and positions change after a removal. Equality compares vertex sets, edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sets and each vertex’s side, not orders.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:15BipartiteGraphs0A5GraphV","symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"BipartiteGraphs"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/BipartiteGraphs\/BipartiteGraph.swi